channels (labeled 'Subscribe').  Upon subscription, these users receive loc=
ation updates ('Friends' location update') through their own WebSocket conn=
ections ('User 2's WS connection,' 'User 3's WS connection,' 'User 4's WS c=
onnection,' and 'User 6's WS connection') within the 'WebSocket Servers' la=
yer, effectively enabling real-time location sharing.  The dashed boxes vis=
ually group the WebSocket servers and the Redis Pub/Sub components." loadin=
